{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1350865,"ns":0,"title":"Affine Lie algebra","extract":"In mathematics, an affine Lie algebra is an infinite-dimensional Lie algebra that is constructed in a canonical fashion out of a finite-dimensional simple Lie algebra. Given an affine Lie algebra, one can also form the associated affine Kac-Moody algebra, as described below.","description":"Type of Kac–Moody algebras","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}